 Evaluations automatically assess the quality of your LLM [generations](/docs/ai-observability/generations). PostHog supports three types of evaluations:
 
-- **LLM-as-a-judge** – Uses an LLM to score each generation against a prompt you define, returning a pass/fail result with reasoning. Great for nuanced, subjective checks like tone, helpfulness, or hallucination detection.
-- **Code-based (Hog)** – Runs deterministic code you write against each generation, returning a pass/fail result. Great for rule-based checks like format validation, keyword detection, or length limits. Free to run with no LLM cost.
+- **LLM-as-a-judge** – Uses an LLM to score each generation against a prompt you define, returning a pass/fail result, a numeric score, or categories, with reasoning. Great for nuanced, subjective checks like tone, helpfulness, or hallucination detection.
+- **Code-based (Hog)** – Runs deterministic code you write against each generation, returning a pass/fail result, a numeric score, or categories. Great for rule-based checks like format validation, keyword detection, or length limits. Free to run with no LLM cost.
 - **Sentiment analysis** – Classifies the sentiment of user messages as positive, neutral, or negative using a local ML model. Great for monitoring how users feel during conversations with your AI features. Free to run with no LLM cost.
 
